# app/data/item-templates.bin is 13 MB of packed item artwork, and its first
# NUL byte is 2.1 MB in - far past the 8000 bytes git reads to decide whether a
# file is binary. So git classifies it as TEXT, and anyone who clones with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) gets CRLF conversion applied
# to it: 134,171 lone LF bytes become CRLF, the file grows by that much, and it
# no longer parses.
#
# This line is what stops that. Verified by cloning with core.autocrlf=true and
# comparing the SHA-256 - identical, byte for byte.
*.bin binary
